      "notes": [
        "El Male Rachamim as printed in the Metsudah Yom Kippur Machzor (Ashkenaz), Hebrew column. Two paragraphs: for a man (שֶׁהָלַךְ לְעוֹלָמוֹ ...) and for a woman (שֶׁהָלְכָה לְעוֹלָמָהּ ...). Key \"el-male-rachamim\" = man, \"el-male-rachamim-female\" = woman.",
        "Name slot: its own line (פב\"פ) between \"אֶת נִשְׁמַת\" and the relative clause; flagged slot:\"name\". It abbreviates פלוני בן פלוני; the source prints the same abbreviation for the woman's form (no separate בת/אמה wording).",
        "The Tetragrammaton is printed fully pointed (יְהֹוָה). That is how the source has it; the display layer must decide how to render the Name. It is NOT altered here.",
        "The source is line-per-phrase; each source line is one segment. Nothing in this prayer is marked as a congregation response in the source, so every segment is \"leader\" (the person reciting).",
        "Same Yom Kippur Memorial Services section also holds the Yizkor paragraphs and Av HaRachamim; they are not imported."
